L0-L10 P0: Memory of the World Register, Hereford Mappa Mundi, Ref 2006-32. Summary: only complete large medieval world map for public display; depicts locations/geographic features and also functions as visual encyclopaedia with historical, anthropological, ethnographical, biblical, classical and theological information.
L28-L40 P0: Identity and description: Hereford Mappa Mundi, medieval map of the world on one vellum sheet, dated c.1290-c1310; around 500 illustrations include cities/towns, biblical events, plants/animals/birds/fish, peoples and classical mythology.
L41-L57 P0-1: At the top Christ is depicted in judgement; the map presents the place of humankind in a divinely ordered worldview. It is the only complete surviving example of a once more common display-map genre; the Catalan world map and portolan charts have different purposes. Hereford is a surviving synthesis of classical knowledge and medieval worldview.
L58-L84 P1-2: Assessment describes medieval European representation, geographic awareness and didactic/spiritual subject and theme.
L85-L101 P2: Form/style and rarity; unique surviving map genre.
L102-L129 P2: Ownership, custodian, access and legal details.
L130-L149 P3: Management, consultation and preservation.
L150-L154 P3: Lodgement, signed 31 March 2006.
L155-L203 P4: Appendix management plan; storage, conservation, fire prevention, emergency, budget and access.

